1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,580
(Sheldon:)Are you monitoring
your circadian rhythms

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,790
(Sheldon:)in order to identify your periods
of maximum mental acuity?

3
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,620
(Sheldon:)I did that one summer.

4
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:09,420
(Sheldon:)Ah, youth.

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:13,290
(Amy:)No, I experienced some
distressing symptoms last night,

6
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,200
(Amy:)so I'm checking
my vital signs every hour.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,230
(Sheldon:)I'd be happy to create a chart

8
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:19,930
(Sheldon:)and participate in a
differential diagnosis.

9
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:22,000
(Amy:)Oh, that sounds like fun.

10
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:26,510
(Sheldon:)All right.

11
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:28,110
(Sheldon:)What were the symptoms?

12
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:32,010
(Amy:)Elevated heart rate,
moist palms, dry mouth

13
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:34,980
(Amy:)and localized
vascular throbbing.

14
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:39,650
(Sheldon:)Localized to what region?

15
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:43,320
(Amy:)Ears and genitalia.

16
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:45,560
(Amy:)Interesting.

17
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:48,260
(Sheldon:)Not body parts
that usually team up.

18
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,030
(Sheldon:)What about
environmental factors?

19
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:54,940
(Sheldon:)Describe the scene for me.

20
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,200
(Amy:)I was sitting in a restaurant
with Penny and Bernadette,

21
00:00:57,210 --> 00:01:00,070
(Amy:)drinking water-- carbonated
as it was a special occasion.

